xnu 0267: 1024 bytes of boot arguments, because the tail was being dropped

The cmdline this port boots with passed 608 bytes when the first canvas
measurement flags were added, and nothing said so: the shim copies the payload
header's `cmdline[BOOT_LINE_LENGTH]` byte for byte into `boot_args.CommandLine`,
`tools/mkpayload.py` cuts the string to the same size, and `kern.bootargs` is
`strlcpy(..., BOOT_LINE_LENGTH)`, so every reader saw the first 607 characters
and no more. That is invisible until a flag near the end has to work: ring225
booted with `mondriandumpicon=1 mondrianiconset=1`, the dump ran, and the
artwork pass never did, because its flag sat just past the cut. Who iBoot's
limit was sized for no longer matters here -- the shim is the bootloader -- and
i386 already uses 1024.

The shim, tools/mkpayload.py, tools/qemu-ios.py and this header have to agree on
the number, and the payload header's segment table moves with it.

diff --git a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/boot.h b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/boot.h
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/boot.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/boot.h
@@ -22,8 +22,19 @@
  *
  * This value matches iBoot's IBOOT_MAX_ENV_VAR_DATA_SIZE.
  * There are no iBoot headers so have to duplicate it here for now.
+ *
+ * mondrian: iBoot is not in this path any more, the shim is the bootloader and
+ * it fills CommandLine from the payload header, so this is *our* limit and not
+ * Apple's. At 608 a boot whose arguments include a few measurement flags lost
+ * its tail silently: the shim and the payload header cut the string at the same
+ * size, and `kern.bootargs` is only ever 607 characters, so a flag near the end
+ * simply did not exist for the hook that was looking for it (measured, ring225:
+ * `mondrianiconset=1` was absent while `mondriandumpicon=1`, seventeen bytes
+ * earlier, was there). 1024 is what i386 uses and it leaves room for the
+ * measurement flags; the shim, tools/mkpayload.py and tools/qemu-ios.py carry
+ * the same number and have to change together.
  */
-#define BOOT_LINE_LENGTH        608
+#define BOOT_LINE_LENGTH        1024
 
 /*
  * Video information..
